# Semgrep path exclusions — keep `semgrep scan --config auto` (see
# .github/workflows/security.yml) focused on the PRODUCTION attack surface.
#
# THIS FILE IS PINNED. Every pattern below has a matching entry, with a written
# rationale, in scripts/ci/tests/test_semgrep_scan_scope.py — adding or removing
# a line here fails CI until that registry is updated too. It is a scan-SCOPE
# definition, NOT a risk acceptance: excluding a file must mean "this is not
# shipped", never "this finding is inconvenient". A finding you want to accept
# is a register entry in shipwright_accepted_risks.yaml instead.
#
# Only four pattern shapes are supported, because the CI matcher implements
# exactly those: `*.ext` (basename), `dir/` (any depth), `a/b/` (anchored dir),
# `a/b/c.ext` (anchored file). A negation, `**`, a character class or a leading
# slash is REJECTED rather than silently misread.
#
# Test/E2E specs, one-off POC scripts, and the Shipwright SDLC doc tree are
# not shipped at runtime; scanning them only produced audit-rule noise that
# GitHub code-scanning then inflated to "high" (111 high / 19 medium), while
# the dashboard ingest graded the same findings "low" — the divergence that
# triage item trg-4c0ab9b0 surfaced. Production-code false positives are
# suppressed inline with `// nosemgrep: <rule>` + a justification comment.
# See iterate-2026-06-30-semgrep-fp-suppression.

# --- Test + E2E suites (Vitest unit/integration + Playwright) ---
*.test.ts
*.test.tsx
*.test.mjs
*.spec.ts
*.spec.tsx
client/e2e/

# --- One-off / POC + dev-time scripts (not part of the runtime server) ---
#
# NAMED FILE BY FILE, not as `server/scripts/`. That blanket exclusion was
# wrong: copy-assets.mjs in the same directory is the second half of
# `npm run build` ("tsc && node scripts/copy-assets.mjs") and copies
# src/config -> dist/config, without which `node dist/index.js` ENOENTs. It
# shapes the SHIPPED artifact and must stay in scan scope. A NEW file added to
# this directory is therefore scanned until someone excludes it deliberately —
# which is the safe default. (Codex cross-check on triage trg-ab54e3d1.)
server/scripts/regen-launch-payload-fixtures.py
server/scripts/regen-triage-fixtures.py
server/scripts/sdk-poc.ts

# --- Shipwright SDLC docs, planning, compliance artifacts (not code) ---
.shipwright/

# --- Build output / vendored deps (node_modules is default-ignored; explicit) ---
dist/
build/
node_modules/
